, the record on Monroe County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 53% of normal in July to August and 38% in November to December. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 47% and March to April at 59%. On grid 17855 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 is 25.1, and that number can still change.</p>"}
